/Title (Rising as the highest peak of Nepal's remote Api-Nampa massif, Api Himal is one of the country's least-climbed 7,000er. First ascended by a Japanese expedition in 1960, it has seen only a handful of successful summits, with the last recorded ascent achieved in 2015 by a Japanese Trio climbing in elegant alpine-style.)
